:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPts val="2800"/><a:buFont typeface="Calibri"/><a:buChar char="•"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="2800" u="none" cap="none" strike="noStrike"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>Ammonia is captured by a series of transaminations.</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p><a:p><a:pPr indent="-342900" lvl="0" marL="342900" marR="0" rtl="0" algn="l"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="560"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPts val="2800"/><a:buFont typeface="Calibri"/><a:buChar char="•"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="2800" u="none" cap="none" strike="noStrike"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>Transaminations allow transfer of an amine to a common metabolite (e.g., </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="1" lang="en-US" sz="2800" u="none" cap="none" strike="noStrike"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>α</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="2800" u="none" cap="none" strike="noStrike"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>-ketoglutarate) and generate a traffickable amino acid (e.g., glutamate).</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr descr="Image (a) begins at the top with amino acids from ingested protein (in a pink box), which points to H3N (with a plus on top of the N). This is in a pink box, and is located in the liver. In the liver box, cellular protein has reversible arrows pointing down to amino acids, where C bonds up to COO-, left to H3N (mentioned above), down to R, and right to H. An arrow points right from this to alpha-keto acids, where C bonds up to COO-, down to R, and double bonds right to O. Below the arrow is a curved arrow, where the arc touches the line pointing right. It points from alpha-ketoglutarate to glutamate. Alpha-ketoglutarate begins with C, which bonds up to COO-, double bonds right to O, and down to CH2, which bonds down to CH2, which bonds down to COO-. Glutamate starts with C, bonds up to COO-, left to H3N (with a plus above the N, and in a pink box), right to H, and down to CH2, which bonds down to CH2, which bonds down to COO-. To the right, outside the liver box, is a pink box with alanine from muscle. This box points left, back into the liver box, to alpha-ketoglutarate, where C bonds right to H, up to COO-, down to CH3, and left to H3N (in a pink box, with a plus sign over N). An arrow from this points left back to glutamate. A waved arrow points from alpha-ketoglutarate through the arrow pointing left, down to pyruvate. Pyruvate begins with C, which bonds up to COO-, double bonds right to O, and down to CH3. Below and left of pyruvate is glutamine, which begins with C, which bonds up to COO-, left to H3N (with a plus over N), right to H, and down to CH2, which bonds down to CH2, which bonds down to C, which double bonds down and left to O and bonds down and right to NH2 (in a pink box). To the right of the liver box is a pink box with glutamine from muscle and other tissues, which has arrow pointing left to glutamine. An arrow above glutamine points up to glutamate. Another arrow jets left off this arrow to NH4+. Above this is a curved arrow from glutamate pointing to alpha-ketoglutarate. This has another arrow jetting off to the same NH4+ in a the pink box. This NH4+ points down to a pink box outside of the liver box with NH4+, urea, or uric acid. " id="179" name="Google Shape;179;p25"/><p:cNvPicPr preferRelativeResize="0"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvPicPr><p:blipFill rotWithShape="1"><a:blip r:embed="rId3"><a:alphaModFix/></a:blip><a:srcRect b="0" l="0" r="0" t="0"/><a:stretch/></p:blipFill><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="0" y="842962"/><a:ext cx="4876800" cy="5991225"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln><a:noFill/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:pic></p:spTree></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping/></p:clrMapOvr></p:sld>